faq:
  - q: "Does LinkedIn cold outreach work for job searching?"
    a: "Yes — with the right approach. InMail response rates for well-targeted, specific messages average 18–25% vs. 3–5% for generic messages. The key: reference something specific about them or their company, be brief, and do not lead with your ask."
  - q: "What is the best cold outreach message for job search?"
    a: "The TIARA framework: Trigger (why you're reaching out now), Identity (who you are in one line), Ask (a small, easy ask — not a job), Rationale (why you chose them specifically), Appreciation (brief close). Example for a hiring manager: 'I noticed [Company] is expanding its [team/product area] — saw the recent announcement. I'm a [level] [role] with specific experience in [relevant area]. Would love 15 minutes to learn more about the direction. No agenda other than curiosity.'"
  - q: "How many cold outreach messages should I send per day?"
    a: "Quality over volume. 5–10 highly targeted messages per day, each with a specific hook, outperforms 50 generic messages. Track responses. If your acceptance or response rate is below 15%, the message or targeting needs adjustment."
  - q: "Should I cold message a hiring manager directly?"
    a: "Yes — this is often more effective than applying through the ATS and waiting. Find the hiring manager on LinkedIn (title usually has 'Engineering Manager,' 'Director of Product,' etc.), view their profile to find a specific hook, send a brief message. Conversion rate is lower than a referral but significantly higher than an ATS application."
